From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, propsys, msvcp140, msvcr*, ucrtbase, shell32, comctl32: DbgPrompt, VariantCompare, _Throw_Cpp_error, _invoke_watson, selected icons

Stubs, as documented now:

- ntdll DbgPrompt ("@ stub"): the prompt goes out as DbgPrint's text
  does; with no kernel debugger to answer, nothing comes back (0).
- propsys VariantCompare ("@ stub"): PropVariantCompareEx of the values,
  with the default unit and flags.
- msvcp140 std::_Throw_Cpp_error ("@ stub"): throws std::system_error for
  the thread library's error codes (busy, invalid argument, no such
  process, not enough memory, operation not permitted, resource deadlock
  would occur, resource unavailable try again), as _Throw_C_error does
  for the C ones.
- _invoke_watson ("@ stub" in ucrtbase and msvcr80 to msvcr120): the
  process ends as __fastfail(FAST_FAIL_INVALID_ARG) does, a fail-fast
  STATUS_STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN.
- SHGetFileInfo SHGFI_SELECTED (a FIXME) gives the icon blended with the
  highlight colour; comctl32's ImageList_GetIcon ignored its style flags
  and now draws the blends and overlays asked for.

Gate: test/smallstubs3-gate.sh (on Xvfb, test/smallstubs3-probe.c).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_NOT_SELECTED (shell32/shell32_main.c).
